WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:03.960
- [Mark] All right, so what is your name?

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:05.423
- Leviticus Brown.

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:07.340
- [Mark] Leviticus Brown, very good name.

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.750
- Yeah.

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:09.780
- [Mark] And where are you from?

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:10.640
- Harlem, New York.

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:11.473
- [Mark] Harlem?
- Yeah.

00:00:11.473 --> 00:00:13.118
- [Mark] And how long
have you been out here?

00:00:13.118 --> 00:00:14.690
- Since 1991.

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:17.070
I exited the US Navy.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:18.940
I'm a Persian Gulf War vet.

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:20.680
Been high since 1991.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:22.480
I have one son

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:23.313
and

00:00:24.581 --> 00:00:26.731
I'm from a family of
alcoholics, of course.

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:31.150
I don't know, maybe
alcoholism is hereditary or

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:34.680
I don't know, if it's just
learned behavior, but anyway...

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:36.320
- [Mark] Is alcohol your issue?

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:37.639
- Alcohol and drugs.

00:00:37.639 --> 00:00:38.472
- [Mark] And drugs too?

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:41.320
- Initially it was alcohol.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:43.070
I was an alcoholic from,

00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:44.980
well my dad was an alcoholic.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:47.380
So I just learned some
behavior traits from him.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:51.840
He died from cirrhosis
of the liver, of course,

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:53.043
at the age of 52.

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:55.470
That was the last time
I've been in New York.

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:58.573
I haven't seen my mom since 1991.

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:01.060
So it's been a long time.

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:02.920
She's very upset with me about it

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.870
but there's issues going
on in my life where

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:10.230
I feel that I don't wanna
take them back home to her.

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:12.100
All my siblings and family members,

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.983
all of them are back in New York.

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:18.300
Started out as an alcoholic.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:19.910
After I got out the Navy,

00:01:19.910 --> 00:01:21.700
I liked going to bars.

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:22.860
The Red Onion,

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:25.090
the Golden Frog.

00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:26.187
Hey, I thought I was a great dancer,

00:01:26.187 --> 00:01:28.380
I thought I was fantastic

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:30.210
on the dance floor when I got drunk,

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:32.680
drinking them Long Island iced teas.

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:33.860
But it came to the point to where

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:36.293
I started crashing my car into poles.

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:38.130
Instead of hitting the brakes,

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:39.920
I was hitting the gas pedal.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:40.753
And,

00:01:41.715 --> 00:01:44.060
why, one day I was driving down the street

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:46.770
and I had a 40 ounce of beer in my lap

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:48.993
and schools was getting out, you know?

00:01:51.655 --> 00:01:52.904
I reached down, the beer spilled,

00:01:52.904 --> 00:01:54.350
I reached down to pick up the beer

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:57.600
and I heard a big thump
(rumbles) like, you know,

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:59.870
and I looked at my rear view mirror,

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:02.270
I saw a lady laying in
the middle of the street.

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:05.533
I stomped on the gas pedal

00:02:05.533 --> 00:02:07.810
and broke the windshield, just ran,

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:10.260
and just threw the bottle away,

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:11.093
bought some gum,

00:02:11.093 --> 00:02:12.800
thought about it for a second.

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:13.900
And I thought maybe

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.950
it would be difficult for
me to live with myself

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:18.860
not knowing what had
happened to this person.

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:22.130
I went back to the scene
and it was a teacher.

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:24.250
She had just retired that day

00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:26.060
and they had a retirement celebration

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:27.210
